ied as \"active ulcers\" according to the North American working group definition: epithelial denudation is clearly Visible at one place and the bed of de-epithelialized ulcer can be seen; Ulcerations distal to the proximal interphalangeal joint, not associated with calcinosis or bony relief.\"\n                            },\n                            \"right\": {\n                              \"AND\": {\n                                \"left\": {\n                                  \"raw_text\": \"Ulcers whose major axis measured with the electronic caliper is ≥ 2 mm\"\n                                },\n                                \"right\": {\n                                  \"AND\": {\n                                    \"left\": {\n                                      \"raw_text\": \"Age greater than or equal to 18 years\"\n                                    },\n                                    \"right\": {\n                                      \"AND\": {\n                                        \"left\": {\n                                          \"raw_text\": \"Existence of a contraceptive method for women of reproductive age\"\n                                        },\n                                        \"right\": {\n                                          \"AND\": {\n                                            \"left\": {\n                                              \"raw_text\": \"A person who is or is a beneficiary of social security\"\n                                            },\n                                            \"right\": {\n                                              \"AND\": {\n                                                \"left\": {\n                                                  \"raw_text\": \"Informed and signed consent signed by the patient or his / her legal representative.\"\n                                                }\n                                              }\n                  